{"files":[{"content":"#include <ctype.h>\n#include <limits.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n  int id;\n  float value;\n  size_t edge_begin;\n  size_t edge_count;\n} Node;\n\ntypedef struct {\n  int id;\n  int index;\n} IdIndex;\n\nstatic void fail(void) {\n  fputs(\"Error!\", stderr);\n  fputc(10, stderr);\n  exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n}\n\nstatic void *checked_malloc(size_t size) {\n  void *result = malloc(size);\n  if (result == NULL && size != 0)\n    fail();\n  return result;\n}\n\nstatic void *checked_realloc(void *memory, size_t size) {\n  void *result = realloc(memory, size);\n  if (result == NULL && size != 0)\n    fail();\n  return result;\n}\n\nstatic char *read_line(FILE *stream) {\n  size_t capacity = 128;\n  size_t length = 0;\n  char *line = checked_malloc(capacity);\n  int ch;\n\n  while ((ch = fgetc(stream)) != EOF && ch != 10) {\n    if (length >= capacity - 1) {\n      if (capacity > SIZE_MAX / 2)\n        fail();\n      capacity *= 2;\n      line = checked_realloc(line, capacity);\n    }\n    line[length++] = (char)ch;\n  }\n\n  if (ch == EOF && length == 0) {\n    free(line);\n    return NULL;\n  }\n  if (length > 0 && line[length - 1] == 13)\n    length--;\n  line[length] = '\\0';\n  return line;\n}\n\nstatic char *skip_space(char *text) {\n  while (*text != '\\0' && isspace((unsigned char)*text))\n    text++;\n  return text;\n}\n\nstatic void append_int(int **values, size_t *count, size_t *capacity,\n                       int value) {\n  if (*count == *capacity) {\n    size_t new_capacity = *capacity == 0 ? 16 : *capacity * 2;\n    if (new_capacity < *capacity || new_capacity > SIZE_MAX / sizeof(**values))\n      fail();\n    *values = checked_realloc(*values, new_capacity * sizeof(**values));\n    *capacity = new_capacity;\n  }\n  (*values)[(*count)++] = value;\n}\n\nstatic int compare_id_index(const void *left, const void *right) {\n  const IdIndex *a = left;\n  const IdIndex *b = right;\n  if (a->id != b->id)\n    return a->id < b->id ? -1 : 1;\n  if (a->index != b->index)\n    return a->index < b->index ? -1 : 1;\n  return 0;\n}\n\nstatic int find_by_id(const IdIndex *ids, int count, int id) {\n  size_t low = 0;\n  size_t high = (size_t)count;\n\n  while (low < high) {\n    size_t middle = low + (high - low) / 2;\n    if (ids[middle].id < id)\n      low = middle + 1;\n    else\n      high = middle;\n  }\n  if (low < (size_t)count && ids[low].id == id)\n    return ids[low].index;\n  return -1;\n}\n\nstatic float cost_from_node(int start, int count, const Node *nodes,\n                            const int *next_node, float *costs,\n                            unsigned char *done, int *path) {\n  size_t path_length = 0;\n  int current = start;\n\n  while (current >= 0 && !done[current]) {\n    if (path_length >= (size_t)count)\n      fail();\n    path[path_length++] = current;\n    current = next_node[current];\n  }\n\n  float total = current >= 0 ? costs[current] : 0.0f;\n  while (path_length > 0) {\n    int node = path[--path_length];\n    total = nodes[node].value + total;\n    costs[node] = total;\n    done[node] = 1;\n  }\n  return costs[start];\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n  char *header = read_line(stdin);\n  if (header == NULL)\n    fail();\n\n  char *cursor = skip_space(header);\n  char *end = NULL;\n  long count_value = strtol(cursor, &end, 10);\n  if (end == cursor || count_value < 0 || count_value > INT_MAX)\n    fail();\n  int count = (int)count_value;\n\n  char *query_text = skip_space(end);\n  size_t query_length = strlen(query_text);\n  if (query_length == SIZE_MAX)\n    fail();\n  char *computelist = checked_malloc(query_length + 1);\n  memcpy(computelist, query_text, query_length + 1);\n  free(header);\n\n  if ((size_t)count > SIZE_MAX / sizeof(Node) ||\n      (size_t)count > SIZE_MAX / sizeof(IdIndex) ||\n      (size_t)count > SIZE_MAX / sizeof(int) ||\n      (size_t)count > SIZE_MAX / sizeof(float))\n    fail();\n\n  Node *nodes = count > 0\n                    ? checked_malloc((size_t)count * sizeof(*nodes))\n                    : NULL;\n  int *raw_neighbors = NULL;\n  size_t raw_count = 0;\n  size_t raw_capacity = 0;\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n    char *line = read_line(stdin);\n    if (line == NULL)\n      fail();\n\n    cursor = skip_space(line);\n    long id_value = strtol(cursor, &end, 10);\n    if (end == cursor || id_value < INT_MIN || id_value > INT_MAX)\n      fail();\n    cursor = skip_space(end);\n    float value = strtof(cursor, &end);\n    if (end == cursor)\n      fail();\n    cursor = skip_space(end);\n\n    nodes[i].id = (int)id_value;\n    nodes[i].value = value;\n    nodes[i].edge_begin = raw_count;\n    nodes[i].edge_count = 0;\n\n    char *token = strtok(cursor, \" \");\n    while (token != NULL) {\n      append_int(&raw_neighbors, &raw_count, &raw_capacity, atoi(token));\n      nodes[i].edge_count++;\n      token = strtok(NULL, \" \");\n    }\n    free(line);\n  }\n\n  IdIndex *ids = count > 0\n                     ? checked_malloc((size_t)count * sizeof(*ids))\n                     : NULL;\n  for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n    ids[i].id = nodes[i].id;\n    ids[i].index = i;\n  }\n  if (count > 1)\n    qsort(ids, (size_t)count, sizeof(*ids), compare_id_index);\n\n  int *edges = raw_neighbors;\n  for (size_t i = 0; i < raw_count; i++)\n    edges[i] = find_by_id(ids, count, edges[i]);\n\n  int *next_node = count > 0\n                       ? checked_malloc((size_t)count * sizeof(*next_node))\n                       : NULL;\n  float *costs = count > 0\n                     ? checked_malloc((size_t)count * sizeof(*costs))\n                     : NULL;\n  unsigned char *done = count > 0\n                            ? calloc((size_t)count, sizeof(*done))\n                            : NULL;\n  if (count > 0 && done == NULL)\n    fail();\n  int *path = count > 0\n                  ? checked_malloc((size_t)count * sizeof(*path))\n                  : NULL;\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n    float maximum = 0.0f;\n    int selected = -1;\n    size_t edge_end = nodes[i].edge_begin + nodes[i].edge_count;\n    for (size_t edge = nodes[i].edge_begin; edge < edge_end; edge++) {\n      int neighbor = edges[edge];\n      if (neighbor >= 0 && maximum < nodes[neighbor].value) {\n        maximum = nodes[neighbor].value;\n        selected = neighbor;\n      }\n    }\n    if (selected >= 0 && nodes[selected].id != -1)\n      next_node[i] = selected;\n    else\n      next_node[i] = -1;\n  }\n\n  char *query = strtok(computelist, \" \");\n  while (query != NULL) {\n    int node = find_by_id(ids, count, atoi(query));\n    float result = node >= 0\n                       ? cost_from_node(node, count, nodes, next_node, costs,\n                                        done, path)\n                       : 0.0f;\n    printf(\"%s: %f%c\", query, result, 10);\n    query = strtok(NULL, \" \");\n  }\n\n  free(path);\n  free(done);\n  free(costs);\n  free(next_node);\n  free(edges);\n  free(ids);\n  free(nodes);\n  free(computelist);\n  return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/graph.c"}],"hypothesis":"Replacing per-node neighbor strings and repeated linear ID scans with compact contiguous adjacency, a sorted ID index, and cached iterative path sums may improve locality and reduce whole-program work while preserving traversal and output semantics.","notes":"One source-file experiment; no commands or measurements were run. The sorted index keeps the first input node for duplicate IDs, unresolved neighbors are skipped, and the selected-neighbor scan retains input order and strict-greater tie behavior.","sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Store parsed neighbor references in a contiguous adjacency array and record per-node edge ranges instead of copying and tokenizing neighbor strings during each traversal.","Build an ID-sorted index with input position as the tie-breaker, resolving neighbor IDs once while preserving first-match behavior for duplicates and skipping missing IDs.","Precompute each node's selected next node and iteratively cache path sums, retaining the original positive-value selection rule, neighbor tie order, and output token spelling."]}